column2:
This is from the Cursor blog [1] linked in the description, but repeating it here in case it's useful to anyone:<p>------<p><i>Check whether you are impacted</i><p>The malicious extension appends the attacker's public key, labeled svc-telemetry, to your SSH authorized keys. To check for it:<p>On macOS, run:<p><pre><code>   grep -qs svc-telemetry ~/.ssh/authorized_keys && echo "svc-telemetry key found" || echo "No key found; machine not impacted"
</code></pre>
On Windows, run in PowerShell:<p><pre><code>   $files = "$HOME\.ssh\authorized_keys", "C:\ProgramData\ssh\administrators_authorized_keys" | Where-Object { Test-Path $_ }
   if ($files -and (Select-String svc-telemetry $files)) { "svc-telemetry key found" } else { "No key found; machine not impacted" }
</code></pre>
------<p>[1] <a href="https://cursor.com/blog/claude-code-extension-security-notice" rel="nofollow">https://cursor.com/blog/claude-code-extension-security-notic...</a>
